WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:09.426 --> 00:00:11.345
Come on! Come on! Let's do this!

2
00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:12.387
Let's go! Let's go! Let's go!

3
00:00:12.471 --> 00:00:13.639
Go! Go! Go!

4
00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:49.383
Rupert and I bought this
on our fifth anniversary.

5
00:00:50.175 --> 00:00:52.344
Well, you have exquisite taste.

6
00:00:53.595 --> 00:00:54.596
Do you want it?

7
00:00:55.556 --> 00:00:59.142
But it's a Hockney.
It must be worth a million pounds.

8
00:00:59.977 --> 00:01:01.979
Good point. You should've said yes.

9
00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:03.856
-Auction pile, please.
-Right away, ma'am.

10
00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:11.864
So, Mrs. Mannion--

11
00:01:11.947 --> 00:01:14.199
Excuse me. Ms. Welton.

12
00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:16.577
George is here.

13
00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.245
If he's here, why isn't he here?

14
00:01:18.328 --> 00:01:20.956
Yes. Good point.

15
00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:22.541
George.

16
00:01:23.125 --> 00:01:25.294
-Higgy boy.
-Good one.

17
00:01:25.919 --> 00:01:28.046
Hey. I love what you've done to the place.

18
00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.924
Did you do it yourself
or get some poof to help you?

19
00:01:31.008 --> 00:01:33.135
I could ask the same of your hair. Please.

20
00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.221
She's a cheeky one, isn't she?

21
00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:39.099
Right, love.
Listen, I've got training in a minute.

22
00:01:39.183 --> 00:01:42.728
So whatever it is
you need to get off your impressive chest,

23
00:01:42.811 --> 00:01:44.479
-let me have it.
-Of course.

24
00:01:44.563 --> 00:01:45.564
You're fired.

25
00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:47.024
Yeah, right.

26
00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:49.651
And I'll be buying out
the remainder of your contract. So...

27
00:01:51.195 --> 00:01:52.821
Wish you the best of luck.

28
00:01:54.573 --> 00:01:56.116
Fired? What the fuck for?

29
00:01:58.243 --> 00:02:00.954
I suppose I could go for
any number of reasons, really.

30
00:02:01.747 --> 00:02:03.332
Your casual misogyny, for one.

31
00:02:03.415 --> 00:02:05.250
-What?
-I know, it's a big word.

32
00:02:05.334 --> 00:02:06.960
Ask one of your daughters what it means.

33
00:02:07.044 --> 00:02:08.628
Or perhaps it's your performance,

34
00:02:08.711 --> 00:02:12.633
having led this team through
yet another remarkably average season.

35
00:02:12.716 --> 00:02:15.302
Or maybe it's because you insist
on wearing those tiny shorts

36
00:02:15.385 --> 00:02:17.137
that force me to see
one of your testicles.

37
00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:19.681
And there's the other one.

38
00:02:20.349 --> 00:02:21.433
Liam and Noel.

39
00:02:22.059 --> 00:02:23.519
Though, perhaps not an oasis.

40
00:02:23.602 --> 00:02:26.188
Still, if I'm being
completely honest, George,

41
00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:29.525
you're fired because I'm the owner now,
and I don't like you.

42
00:02:31.109 --> 00:02:32.945
Now do piss off, you fat twat.

43
00:02:36.532 --> 00:02:37.991
Hey, Higgy boy.

44
00:02:38.075 --> 00:02:39.493
What do you think's worse?

45
00:02:39.576 --> 00:02:43.747
Your husband cheating on you
or being the last to know?

46
00:02:46.708 --> 00:02:48.961
Is there someone that could pop out
and fetch me a salad?

47
00:02:50.629 --> 00:02:53.006
Nothing with raisins in it, please.

48
00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:54.216
Fuck you.

49
00:02:54.883 --> 00:02:58.262
So, what to do as far as new managers go?

50
00:02:58.345 --> 00:03:00.889
Shall I prepare a list of candidates?

51
00:03:00.973 --> 00:03:03.642
No. That won't be necessary.

52
00:03:08.438 --> 00:03:11.733
This is a bit of surprising news
from the other side of the Atlantic.

53
00:03:11.817 --> 00:03:14.611
AFC Richmond announced
the hiring of their new manager,

54
00:03:14.695 --> 00:03:16.947
one Theodore "Ted" Lasso.

55
00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:21.410
Recently, it was Coach Lasso leading
the Division II Wichita State Shockers

56
00:03:21.493 --> 00:03:24.329
to their first ever national title
in American football.

57
00:03:24.413 --> 00:03:26.915
He took the Shockers
from a garbage program

58
00:03:26.999 --> 00:03:29.918
all the way to the promised land
in his very first season as head coach.

59
00:03:30.002 --> 00:03:34.006
But for a lot of us, that's not how
Ted Lasso found his way into our hearts,

60
00:03:34.089 --> 00:03:35.591
certainly not into our living rooms.

61
00:03:35.674 --> 00:03:37.217
<i>For me, it'll always be Ted...</i>

62
00:03:38.552 --> 00:03:40.470
<i>celebrating a moment of joy with his team</i>

63
00:03:40.554 --> 00:03:42.764
<i>in a way that you really have to see
to understand.</i>

64
00:03:42.848 --> 00:03:44.349
<i>And then, even when you see it...</i>

65
00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:48.353
<i>I don't necessarily know
that understanding is what we're doing.</i>

66
00:03:50.606 --> 00:03:52.107
Right on, Ted. Do your thing, man.

67
00:03:52.191 --> 00:03:54.526
And good luck
with the most beautiful game.

68
00:03:55.027 --> 00:03:56.236
Do us proud.

69
00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:57.321
Go, 'Murica.

70
00:04:11.502 --> 00:04:12.503
Oi, mate. This you?

71
00:04:12.586 --> 00:04:15.214
-I believe it is, yeah.
-Oh, man! Legend.

72
00:04:15.297 --> 00:04:16.548
Can I get an ussie?

73
00:04:17.966 --> 00:04:19.218
That's dope.

74
00:04:19.301 --> 00:04:21.303
You know, back where I'm from,
we call those selfies.

75
00:04:21.386 --> 00:04:22.638
Well, it's not "myself," yeah?

76
00:04:22.721 --> 00:04:24.389
It's "us," innit? "Ussie."

77
00:04:24.473 --> 00:04:25.891
Yeah. I like that.

78
00:04:25.974 --> 00:04:26.892
Wicked.

79
00:04:27.434 --> 00:04:28.810
You coaching football.

80
00:04:28.894 --> 00:04:31.355
Mate, you are a legend
for doing something so stupid.

81
00:04:31.438 --> 00:04:34.107
I mean, it's mental.
They're gonna fucking murder you.

82
00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:36.985
Well, you know,
I've heard that tune before.

83
00:04:37.069 --> 00:04:38.695
But here I am, still dancing.

84
00:04:38.779 --> 00:04:41.114
-Legend.
-Yeah. Nice meeting you.

85
00:04:45.536 --> 00:04:47.204
What you reading? Another soccer book.

86
00:04:47.287 --> 00:04:48.580
Coach, you are a sponge.

87
00:04:49.206 --> 00:04:51.208
Come on. Hit me with a fun fact.

88
00:04:51.291 --> 00:04:53.919
They don't say "out of bounds."
They say "into touch."

89
00:04:54.002 --> 00:04:56.755
Okay, you owe me five bucks
if I sneak that into a sentence later.

90
00:04:56.839 --> 00:04:58.340
-You're on.
-Okay.

91
00:04:59.883 --> 00:05:02.052
<i>Good evening.
We'll be dimming the cabin shortly.</i>

92
00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:04.346
We should get some sleep.
The jet lag will kill us.

93
00:05:04.429 --> 00:05:06.682
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

94
00:05:09.101 --> 00:05:10.727
Are we nuts for doing this?

95
00:05:11.353 --> 00:05:12.521
Yeah, this is nuts.

96
00:05:12.604 --> 00:05:15.315
Hey, but taking on a challenge
is a lot like riding a horse, isn't it?

97
00:05:15.399 --> 00:05:16.984
If you're comfortable
while you're doing it,

98
00:05:17.067 --> 00:05:18.068
probably doing it wrong.

99
00:05:19.653 --> 00:05:21.697
-Okay, good night, Coach.
-Night, Coach.

100
00:05:25.033 --> 00:05:26.660
Hey, hey, hey!

101
00:05:26.743 --> 00:05:30.122
If we see each other in our dreams,
let's goof around a little bit,

102
00:05:30.205 --> 00:05:32.541
-pretend like we don't know each other.
-You got it, stranger.

103
00:05:32.624 --> 00:05:34.042
Nice.

104
00:06:08.410 --> 00:06:10.495
-You didn't sleep at all?
-Not a wink.

105
00:06:10.579 --> 00:06:12.748
No. My brain just kept on cooking.

106
00:06:12.831 --> 00:06:14.708
At first,
I was thinking about not sleeping.

107
00:06:14.791 --> 00:06:17.419
Then I was thinking about
thinking about not sleeping. And that--

108
00:06:17.503 --> 00:06:18.837
That's never good.

109
00:06:18.921 --> 00:06:19.922
Next thing you know,

110
00:06:20.005 --> 00:06:21.798
they're handing out
warm chocolate chip cookies

111
00:06:21.882 --> 00:06:23.175
and the plane's landing.

112
00:06:23.258 --> 00:06:25.344
I didn't get a cookie. Did you eat mine?

113
00:06:25.427 --> 00:06:27.221
That's not part of the story.
I think this is us right here.

114
00:06:27.304 --> 00:06:28.472
Hey, how ya doin'?

115
00:06:28.555 --> 00:06:29.973
-My name's Ted. What's yours?
-Ollie.

116
00:06:30.057 --> 00:06:31.517
-Ollie. All right.
-Let me get your bags.

117
00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:33.977
No, no, no, Ollie.
We packed 'em, we'll carry 'em.

118
00:06:34.061 --> 00:06:35.979
Love to make a little pit stop though.

119
00:06:36.063 --> 00:06:37.064
Okay. Follow me.

120
00:06:42.110 --> 00:06:43.779
Yeah. There you go.

121
00:06:45.489 --> 00:06:48.158
Coach, I got a feeling
we're not in Kansas anymore, right?

122
00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:51.703
I've never actually said that
when not in Kansas before.

123
00:06:51.787 --> 00:06:53.539
-That's kinda nice.
-Yeah.

124
00:06:54.665 --> 00:06:56.458
Well, thanks for indulging us, Ollie.

125
00:06:56.542 --> 00:06:57.918
Ready to boogie whenever you are.

126
00:06:58.001 --> 00:06:59.503
Okay. That's Tower Bridge.

127
00:06:59.586 --> 00:07:02.422
Right. Not the London Bridge,
'cause this one's still up.

128
00:07:07.094 --> 00:07:08.929
You know how they came up with soccer?

129
00:07:09.012 --> 00:07:10.597
So, these Victorian-era headmasters,

130
00:07:10.681 --> 00:07:13.433
all they wanted to do
was get the boys to stop masturbating.

131
00:07:13.517 --> 00:07:17.187
So they invented a sport where the boys
wouldn't use their hands at all,

132
00:07:17.271 --> 00:07:19.064
and they thought that might do the trick.

133
00:07:19.147 --> 00:07:20.816
I'm not sure if it worked, but...

134
00:07:36.707 --> 00:07:38.584
Feels different, Coach.

135
00:07:38.667 --> 00:07:40.335
I mean, the same, but different.

136
00:07:40.419 --> 00:07:42.421
-Metaphor.
-You know it, baby.

137
00:07:42.504 --> 00:07:43.589
Oi!

138
00:07:43.672 --> 00:07:45.716
Oi! Excuse me!

139
00:07:45.799 --> 00:07:47.009
Oi! Hello!

140
00:07:47.092 --> 00:07:48.427
Off! Off!

141
00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:50.095
Stop touching the grass!

142
00:07:50.179 --> 00:07:52.890
Get off! Get off the pitch!
Stop touching the grass! Please!

143
00:07:52.973 --> 00:07:54.308
-Yep, yep, yep. Yeah.
-Who are you?

144
00:07:54.391 --> 00:07:56.310
I'm Ted Lasso. This is Coach Beard here.

145
00:07:56.393 --> 00:07:58.645
-Oh, God. You're the new manager.
-Yes, sir.

146
00:07:58.729 --> 00:08:00.397
-Take all the grass you want.
-Oh, no--

147
00:08:00.480 --> 00:08:01.732
We just had it cut.
I can go through the garbage.

148
00:08:01.815 --> 00:08:03.942
-I can get you some more.
-That's all right. No need.

149
00:08:04.401 --> 00:08:06.528
-Thank you.
-Yeah.

150
00:08:07.738 --> 00:08:08.989
Yeah.

151
00:08:10.282 --> 00:08:12.492
-Still, we got to get off the grass.
-Yeah, yeah. Absolutely.

152
00:08:12.576 --> 00:08:13.410
Do we apologize?

153
00:08:13.493 --> 00:08:15.120
-Sorry about that, grass.
-Sorry, grass.

154
00:08:16.163 --> 00:08:18.081
So, we're supposed to meet
with a Rebecca Welton.

155
00:08:18.165 --> 00:08:19.416
Yeah, that's where I'm taking you.

156
00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:20.918
Look at this guy. One step ahead.

157
00:08:21.001 --> 00:08:22.920
Hey, what's your name, by the way?

158
00:08:23.003 --> 00:08:24.087
-Me?
-Yeah.

159
00:08:24.171 --> 00:08:25.547
No one ever asks my name.

160
00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:33.138
I mean, whenever you're ready.

161
00:08:33.222 --> 00:08:34.681
Oh, it's Nathan.

162
00:08:34.765 --> 00:08:36.225
Nathan! I love that name.

163
00:08:36.308 --> 00:08:37.392
Hey, love your hot dogs.

164
00:08:38.101 --> 00:08:39.102
Yeah. No, I know.

165
00:08:39.186 --> 00:08:41.605
Good, good.
Y'all got Nathan's hot dogs here?

166
00:08:41.688 --> 00:08:42.688
No.

167
00:08:42.773 --> 00:08:43.774
Okay.

168
00:08:44.983 --> 00:08:46.985
I love this kid. Love him.

169
00:08:47.736 --> 00:08:49.863
I'll introduce you. Big boss.

170
00:08:49.947 --> 00:08:50.948
Here we go.

171
00:08:52.491 --> 00:08:53.492
Hello.

172
00:09:03.836 --> 00:09:06.255
Hey, how y'all doing?
I'm Ted Lasso, your new coach.

173
00:09:06.338 --> 00:09:09.716
-You must be Ms. Welton.
-Please, call me Rebecca.

174
00:09:09.800 --> 00:09:11.009
Ms. Welton's my father.

175
00:09:12.052 --> 00:09:13.637
If that's a joke, I love it.

176
00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:15.514
If not, I cannot wait
to unpack that with you.

177
00:09:16.056 --> 00:09:17.057
This here is Coach Beard.

178
00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:20.269
It is so good
to finally meet you both face-to-face.

179
00:09:20.352 --> 00:09:21.186
Higgins?

180
00:09:21.270 --> 00:09:24.898
Sorry. This is Higgins,
our current director of communications.

181
00:09:24.982 --> 00:09:25.983
Current?

182
00:09:26.066 --> 00:09:29.653
Could you take Coach Beard and get him
their IDs, housing information...

183
00:09:29.736 --> 00:09:31.238
You know, anything they need.

184
00:09:31.321 --> 00:09:34.116
-Wi-Fi password, wet wipes.
-Humidifier. Way ahead of you, Coach.

185
00:09:34.199 --> 00:09:35.284
Thank you.

186
00:09:37.703 --> 00:09:39.705
-Please, take a seat.
-Okay.

187
00:09:40.414 --> 00:09:42.291
-Can I get you something to drink?
-Yes, please.

188
00:09:42.374 --> 00:09:44.334
Didn't get much sleep on the plane,
so anything you got,

189
00:09:44.418 --> 00:09:46.253
a little boost of caffeine,
should do the trick.

190
00:09:46.336 --> 00:09:48.172
You know, mochaccino, Frappuccino...

191
00:09:48.255 --> 00:09:51.008
Any coffee thing, as long as
I can't taste a hint of coffee, is good.

192
00:09:51.091 --> 00:09:52.176
How do you take your tea?

193
00:09:52.801 --> 00:09:54.761
Well, usually I take it
right back to the counter

194
00:09:54.845 --> 00:09:56.805
'cause someone's
made a horrible mistake. But...

195
00:09:56.889 --> 00:09:57.764
when in Rome, right?

196
00:09:58.849 --> 00:10:01.435
Yeah. Look at that. Okay.

197
00:10:05.230 --> 00:10:06.231
Well?

198
00:10:06.315 --> 00:10:09.276
You know, I always figured that tea
was just gonna taste like hot brown water.

199
00:10:09.359 --> 00:10:10.527
And you know what?

200
00:10:10.611 --> 00:10:13.322
I was right.
Yeah, it's horrible. No, thank you.

201
00:10:13.405 --> 00:10:14.656
Welcome to England.

202
00:10:14.740 --> 00:10:16.241
Yeah. "Get used to it, sucker." Right?

203
00:10:16.325 --> 00:10:18.160
Now, would you like a tour?

204
00:10:18.243 --> 00:10:20.621
-I'd love to see Abbey Road.
-Of the club.

205
00:10:20.704 --> 00:10:21.788
Yeah, let's start there.

206
00:10:21.872 --> 00:10:26.877
So, this hall represents
the club's long, albeit modest, history.

207
00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.795
The first match was played in 1897.

208
00:10:28.879 --> 00:10:33.050
During the war, our stadium
was used as a makeshift hospital.

209
00:10:33.133 --> 00:10:34.593
Yeah, some of the locals claim

210
00:10:34.676 --> 00:10:37.679
they still see fallen soldiers
wandering around the pitch.

211
00:10:37.763 --> 00:10:39.139
That's spooky.

212
00:10:39.223 --> 00:10:42.059
-Do you believe in ghosts, Ted?
-I do.

213
00:10:42.142 --> 00:10:45.354
But more importantly, I think they need
to believe in themselves. You know?

214
00:10:46.438 --> 00:10:47.272
Okay.

215
00:10:47.356 --> 00:10:49.900
And this is a wall of our previous owners.

216
00:10:50.442 --> 00:10:52.778
Okay. And now look at this fella up here.

217
00:10:53.445 --> 00:10:55.405
How 'bout the girls
and the champagne and everything?

218
00:10:55.489 --> 00:10:56.949
He looks like a good time.

219
00:10:57.032 --> 00:10:58.242
That's my ex-husband.

220
00:10:58.325 --> 00:11:01.745
Well, good times aren't always
a good time, I've found.

221
00:11:02.287 --> 00:11:03.664
You know, I heard about all that.

222
00:11:03.747 --> 00:11:05.040
How you holding up?

223
00:11:07.209 --> 00:11:08.585
Yeah, hasn't been the easiest year.

224
00:11:08.669 --> 00:11:09.711
Yeah.

225
00:11:10.838 --> 00:11:13.090
-So, we'll need you to speak to the press.
-Yeah.

226
00:11:13.173 --> 00:11:15.843
No, after a couple nights' good sleep,
I'll be happy to do so.

227
00:11:15.926 --> 00:11:18.428
I'm so sorry. I thought you knew.
They're ready for you now.

228
00:11:18.512 --> 00:11:19.346
They're what?

229
00:11:21.807 --> 00:11:23.016
So, without further ado,

230
00:11:23.100 --> 00:11:26.979
the new manager of AFC Richmond,
Ted Lasso!

231
00:11:33.527 --> 00:11:34.778
Okay.

232
00:11:34.862 --> 00:11:36.697
All right. How y'all doing?

233
00:11:40.284 --> 00:11:41.159
There's Coach.

234
00:11:41.243 --> 00:11:43.787
<i>Oluwa</i> Ted, yo.

235
00:11:43.871 --> 00:11:45.163
Look, our coach.

236
00:11:47.207 --> 00:11:48.208
Oi!

237
00:11:48.292 --> 00:11:51.003
If I don't hear silence,
I'm gonna start punching dicks.

238
00:11:52.004 --> 00:11:54.423
One sec. Let me just--
Throat got a little dry.

239
00:11:59.887 --> 00:12:01.805
Did not expect fizzy water there. Sorry.

240
00:12:01.889 --> 00:12:03.807
Look at this twat!

241
00:12:03.891 --> 00:12:05.392
Fucking Yank!

242
00:12:05.475 --> 00:12:07.394
Okay. So, hey.

243
00:12:07.477 --> 00:12:09.855
Why don't we just jump right in?
Anybody got any questions?

244
00:12:11.607 --> 00:12:13.734
Oh, yeah, no. Should've saw that coming.

245
00:12:13.817 --> 00:12:15.777
You know what?
You can put your hands down.

246
00:12:15.861 --> 00:12:16.987
Real quick--

